     <h1 class="title" title="Haflong Hill Station">Haflong</h1>
     <div class="entry-content">
<p>

<img src="https://storage.googleapis.com/createweb/INDIAHILLSTATION.INFO/images/east-india-hill-stations/haflong-hill-station.jpg" title="Haflong hill station" alt="Haflong hill station, hill stations in india, east india hill stations, Haflong" style="width:200px;height:150px" class="thumb alignright"/>
<b>Location:</b> North Cachar Hills, Assam<br />
<b>Area:</b> 12.79 sq.Kms<br />
<b>Significance:</b> Land of Blue Hills<br />
<b>Altitude:</b> 680m above sea level<br />
<b>Climate:</b> Summer 15&#176;C - 28&#176;C, Winter 10&#176;C - 15&#176;C .
<br/>
<b>Best time to visit:</b> October to April</p>     
<b>Main Attractions:</b> Mountains, Tea Garden, Lake, Water front</p>
<p><b>Haflong</b> is a hill station in Assam, situated at an altitude of 680 meters from the sea Haflong Assam is famous for its decorative elements made of blue hills, emerald green rivers, unique orchids such as Vanda Blue and species rare bird. Haflong in Assam is often referred to as a country blue hills. Residents generally include Haflong Himara Mizo and Naga tribes. Pineapples and oranges are grown here in abundance. Haflong is best known for a beach resort on the lake developed into luscious green hills surrounding the city.</p>




